From: Chad Wagner <47257594+wagnerch@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] board: amlogic: add OSMC Vero 4K+ (S905D) defconfig

Add a defconfig and U-Boot device tree include for the OSMC Vero 4K+
(Amlogic S905D, GXL). The board device tree comes from dts/upstream.
This U-Boot is chainloaded (as BL33) from the vendor bootloader.

The board uses an external RTL8211F RGMII PHY, not the SoC's internal
GXL PHY, so CONFIG_PHY_REALTEK is set instead of CONFIG_PHY_MESON_GXL.

CONFIG_VIDEO_MESON is enabled for HDMI output; the GXL VPU/HDMI driver
matches this board's inherited devicetree nodes
(amlogic,meson-gxl-vpu / amlogic,meson-gxl-dw-hdmi).
---
 .../meson-gxl-s905d-vero4k-plus-u-boot.dtsi   |  7 ++
 configs/vero4kplus_defconfig                  | 64 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 71 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/dts/meson-gxl-s905d-vero4k-plus-u-boot.dtsi
 create mode 100644 configs/vero4kplus_defconfig

